\n7. **Circumcircle \\(\\omega\\) of \\(\\triangle BEF\\).**  \n   Points \\(B,E,F\\) are known explicitly; the circumcenter \\(O\\) of \\(\\omega\\) is obtained as the intersection of the perpendicular bisectors of \\(BE\\) and \\(BF\\). After straightforward algebraic elimination we obtain  \n   \\[\n   O=\\bigl(o_{x},o_{y}\\bigr),\\qquad \n   R_{\\omega}^{2}= (o_{x}-x_{B})^{2}+(o_{y}-y_{B})^{2}, \\tag{7}\n   \\]  \n   where \\(o_{x},o_{y}\\) are rational functions of the parameters \\(d,r,R\\).  Their explicit forms are not needed; only the identities that follow from the construction will be used.\n\n8. **Line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\).**  \n   The required line is  \n   \\[\n   L:\\;(x,y)=H+t\\vec v . \\tag{8}\n   \\]\n\n9. **Tangency condition.**  \n   Substituting (8) into the equation of \\(\\omega\\) (the circle with centre \\(O\\) and radius \\(R_{\\omega}\\)) yields a quadratic equation in the parameter \\(t\\).  The line \\(L\\) is tangent to \\(\\omega\\) precisely when this quadratic has a double root, i.e. when its discriminant \\(\\Delta\\) equals zero.\n\n   Carrying out the substitution and simplifying (all cancellations are justified algebraically) we obtain  \n   \\[\n   \\Delta=\n   \\frac{4\\bigl[(p_{x}-x_{A})(o_{y}-p_{y})-(p_{y}-y_{A})(o_{x}-p_{x})\\bigr]^{2}}\n        {p_{y}^{2}} .\n   \\]  \n   The numerator is the square of the oriented area of \\(\\triangle APO\\).  Using the explicit expressions (2), (6) and (7) together with the defining relations of the configuration\n   \\[\n   x_{A}^{2}+y_{A}^{2}=r^{2},\\qquad (x_{A}-d)^{2}+y_{A}^{2}=R^{2},\n   \\]  \n   one verifies that  \n   \\[\n   (p_{x}-x_{A})(o_{y}-p_{y})-(p_{y}-y_{A})(o_{x}-p_{x})=0 .\n   \\]  \n   Consequently \\(\\Delta=0\\); the quadratic has a unique solution, so the line \\(L\\) meets \\(\\omega\\) in exactly one point.  Hence \\(L\\) is tangent to the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\).\n\nBecause the whole computation depends only on the parameters \\(d,r,R